      "description": "Watch Club León vs Real Salt Lake highlights and goals from Leagues Cup on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 26, 2026. The MLS season continued on August 26, 2026, with a fixture that promised to test the tactical discipline of both lineups. As the players took to the field, the anticipation for a decisive performance was palpable among the supporters. Ferreira Breaks the Deadlock The encounter began at a high tempo, with both sides attempting to establish control of the midfield. In the 24th minute, the deadlock was broken when Evander Ferreira found the back of the net, finishing clinically to put his side ahead. The goal forced a reaction from the opposition, significantly increasing the physical intensity of the match. As half-time approached, the contest became increasingly scrappy. Ryan Sailor was shown a yellow card in the 38th minute following a mistimed challenge, reflecting the mounting pressure. Despite attempts to respond before the break, the first half concluded with a narrow lead following three minutes of stoppage time. Tactical Shifts and Late Drama In the second half, the managers looked to refresh their squads through a flurry of substitutions. Between the 59th and 61st minutes, the likes of Kevin Denkey , Danny Musovski , and Nouhou Tolo were introduced to influence the momentum. The tension continued to simmer, resulting in bookings for Bryan Ramirez in the 64th minute and Peter Kingston in the 75th. The defining moment of the comeback arrived following the introduction of Albert Rusnak in the 77th minute. Just six minutes after coming on, Rusnak turned provider for Kalani Rienzi , who made no mistake in leveling the score in the 83rd minute. In the closing stages, both teams managed their defensive lines with further substitutions, including Kee-Hee Kim entering to stabilize the backline, as the match ended in a hard-fought draw after 95 minutes."
